		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Duplex MMDVM hotpot external duplexer]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5014&amp;p=36482#p36482"><![CDATA[
I did range testing a few years ago, comparing a very old hotspot which used a separate RF module , and a new MMDVM HS Duplex hotspot<br><br>The very old hotspot had better Rx sensitivity, but the maximum distance for Rx was still less than 5km<br><br>I checked the schematic for the very old AD7021 module and it used some sort of RF switching chip, so that the RF input and output pins of the AD7021 are more isolated than in the current hotspot designs, in which those pins are capacitive coupled<br><br><br><a href="https://github.com/phl0/MMDVM_HS_Dual_Hat/blob/master/hardware/r1.3/mmdvm_hs_dual_hat.pdf" class="postlink">https://github.com/phl0/MMDVM_HS_Dual_H ... al_hat.pdf</a><br><br>I did wonder whether cutting the Tx path trace on the Rx Ad7021 would improve the Rx sensitivity but I never got around to doing this<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Mar 26, 2025 7:52 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
