		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Duplex MMDVM hotpot external duplexer]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5014&amp;p=36477#p36477"><![CDATA[
Hello Charlie,<br><br>I can't recommend optimizing a duplex hotspot with a duplexer. It won't achieve the desired results.<br>The reason for this is that the ADF7021 RF chip is pretty deaf on 70cm.<br>You can read about an optimization attempt here:<br><a href="https://www.darc.de/fileadmin/filemounts/distrikte/c/ortsverbaende/15/webcontent/DB0MMRgross.pdf" class="postlink">https://www.darc.de/fileadmin/filemount ... Rgross.pdf</a><br><br>To work around this problem, you can use a SIMPLEX HS for YOUR ACTIVE DMR radio traffic, which is much better suited for transmitting. No talkgroups should be statically booked on the Brandmeister Single HS! Unfortunately, Brandmeister doesn't have any drop-in protection for talkgroups that are statically or dynamically booked on the same time slot!<br>I've described this in more detail here:<br><a href="http://tyrofly.at/funk.htm#Bug_Brandmeister_german" class="postlink">http://tyrofly.at/funk.htm#Bug_Brandmeister_german</a><br>For RX, you can then use your duplex HS and activate multiple talkgroups.<br><br>If you need even more TX power on the HS, I can recommend a high-power HS with OpenGD77 firmware.<br><a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#hotspot-mode" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... tspot-mode</a><br><br>73 Alfred, OE7ABH<br>Greetings from Austria!<br><a href="https://tyrofly.at/panos/bad_haering/" class="postlink">https://tyrofly.at/panos/bad_haering/</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1060">oe7abh</a> — Wed Mar 26, 2025 5:16 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
